Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gamma Construction Across Different Sources", "Subchapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999345524972164*^9, 3.99934553005319*^9}, {
  3.9993456931325374`*^9, 
  3.999345693644457*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e819ff62-ed47-4320-afdf-\
a4ae4026636b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["[see -> \nDavis, A.B. & Xu, F. (2014), A Generalized Linear \
Transport Model for Spatially-Correlated Stochastic Media; \nBitterli et al. \
(2018), A Radiative Transfer Framework for Non-Exponential Media\nJarabo, \
Aliaga & Gutierrez 2018 (5.2 - An intuitive local model for \
positively-correlated media); \nWrenninge, Villemin & Hery 2017, Pixar \
Technical Memo 17-07]\n \n",
  FontSize->12,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.5]],
 "The Gamma-mixture construction underlying this entire notebook did not \
originate with Jarabo or Wrenninge -- it traces to Davis & Xu (2014), and is \
used independently by Bitterli et al. (2018) as well."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.999345512210967*^9, {3.9993459769428415`*^9, 3.9993459953601327`*^9}, {
   3.999356806030566*^9, 3.999356807047168*^9}, {3.9993568421097174`*^9, 
   3.9993568651226444`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9135ccd6-53b6-4e31-b897-\
7a5f2b0e01e1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Same  Across Sources", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999345541302805*^9, 
  3.999345547438239*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"066cef12-5f2c-4e99-8e69-\
de1d1e02e9a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The classical, zero-variance limit.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Davis & Xu, verbatim: \[OpenCurlyQuote]In the limit a -> infinity, \
variance vanishes as the PDF becomes degenerate... We then retrieve Beer\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law.\[CloseCurlyQuote] Bitterli et al., verbatim: \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]both the Gaussian and Gamma models reduce to a simple \
exponential when variance v->0 (and hence alpha->infinity).\[CloseCurlyQuote] \
Independent confirmation, in nearly identical language, of the same limit \
already established and corrected earlier in this notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cf5cb-d599-4cef-955c-2b24bc92594e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The sampling formula.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Davis & Xu\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own Eq. 37: s = a*(xi^(-1/a)-1)/sigma. \
Bitterli et al.\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Table 1, Gamma row, sampling column: \
(xi^(-1/alpha)-1)*alpha/mu -- the identical formula under the mu=sigma, \
alpha=a relabeling. Both match nonexp2_sample/neSample exactly, unchanged. \
Two independently-published sources give the same closed-form sampler this \
whole dispatch architecture already relies on."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0b2558c-60b0-4877-aede-8bf438dec58f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The One Genuine Structural Difference: Constant alpha vs. alpha(t)\
\>", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"76f46546-6f1f-4c71-baa1-2ba0875a4f76"],

Cell["\<\
Davis & Xu, and this notebook throughout, treat a as a single fixed constant. \
Bitterli et al. build theirs from a different starting point entirely -- a \
Gaussian model of fractal 1/f^beta noise, following Davis and \
Mineev-Weinstein (2011)\[CloseCurlyQuote]s formal variance derivation -- and \
then replace the (physically invalid, since it permits negative extinction) \
Gaussian with a Gamma matched to the same mean and variance. Because that \
variance genuinely depends on t for general beta, their shape parameter is a \
function alpha(t), not a constant:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4cab2085-4cab-4a05-9eec-70a4c2c1d46f"],

Cell["\<\
alphaOfT[t_, mu_, C_, beta_] := mu^2 / ((C*mu)^(beta+1) * t^(beta-1))\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[60]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9f7032c1-47ea-4c57-bd5b-3ea1be03a1a7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simplify[alphaOfT[t, mu, C, 1]]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[61]:=",ExpressionUUID->"caca0325-dc5d-4604-bc18-ececa5290af5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox["1", 
  SuperscriptBox["C", "2"]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9993453924345803`*^9, 3.9993470376504927`*^9, 
  3.999348125313205*^9, 3.9993505163993835`*^9, 3.9993508946137037`*^9, 
  3.9993512079676466`*^9, 3.9993512484015107`*^9, 3.999355693723605*^9, 
  3.999357100039425*^9, 3.9993578309316053`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[61]=",ExpressionUUID->"a8c615a2-ecc1-48dc-9ced-f0f2173e3a0a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
(* Expect: C^-2, with NO t dependence remaining -- confirmed symbolically \
above *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[62]:=",ExpressionUUID->"684cc99c-8b7a-4bf9-9dd3-5fe10da888d8"],

Cell["\<\
This confirms Bitterli\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own claim precisely: only at \
beta=1, their \[OpenCurlyQuote]pink noise\[CloseCurlyQuote] special case, \
does alpha(t) collapse to a genuine constant, independent of t -- exactly the \
point where their framework reduces to the same single-alpha construction \
Davis & Xu use throughout, and the same one this whole notebook has been \
built on. Away from beta=1, Bitterli\[CloseCurlyQuote]s model is a genuine \
generalization neither Davis & Xu nor this notebook attempts: a Gamma-mixture \
whose own shape parameter is itself a prescribed function of distance, not a \
single number.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c74315f6-58b4-4c68-90c9-6bdc79f44d29"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Mean Free Path Diverges at alpha=1", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9993456347663403`*^9, 
  3.999345635191558*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"592230bf-719d-4704-8c70-\
cc3f3f2c5c5d"],

Cell["\<\
Davis & Xu give a closed form for the mean free path itself, not just the \
transmittance curve:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31cb1a9b-8fc1-46c1-9b89-fc6142625279"],

Cell["meanFreePath[a_, ellInf_] := (a/(a-1)) * ellInf", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[63]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eb7dce15-1bf2-466f-a050-3c92a9fac736"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Limit[meanFreePath[a, ellInf], a -> 1, Direction -> \"FromAbove\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8c30b6ae-8e91-4b04-a509-e6daf73f731f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ellInf", " ", "\[Infinity]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9993453925255666`*^9, 3.999347037715274*^9, 
  3.9993481253679247`*^9, 3.999350516445386*^9, 3.999350894655476*^9, 
  3.999351208021551*^9, 3.999351248439989*^9, 3.9993556937625685`*^9, 
  3.9993571000833054`*^9, 3.999357830971717*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[64]=",ExpressionUUID->"2d9e1d26-6af2-4e01-a9f8-531e2a1df628"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["(* Expect: Infinity *)", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[65]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a01c5a22-4bf3-40a6-b4af-e91abf4e6417"],

Cell["\<\
At exactly the identity point this whole notebook is built around, the \
distribution\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own mean does not exist. Not merely \
heavy-tailed -- the tail is heavy enough that the expected free-flight \
distance is infinite. A third characterization of alpha=1, alongside CV=1 and \
the exponential-rate reduction already established, and independently \
confirmed by direct integration of nePdf earlier in the derivation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5a86757-5264-4122-81cd-7644bc4a0c21"],

Cell["Null", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[66]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9225fc23-5e88-46a0-b421-ec0b767b1874"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["This Is Exactly the Lomax Distribution", "Subchapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9993456843710585`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e9cd4031-ffc2-4c91-87fb-\
e30564849706"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["[see -> Lomax, K.S. (1954), Business Failures: \
Another Example of the Analysis of Failure Data, Journal of the American \
Statistical Association]",
 FontSize->12,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0.5]]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9993457235590115`*^9, 
  3.999345725118601*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"772fa22a-80e9-4acf-a5fa-\
bc9385595292"],

Cell["\<\
The Lomax distribution (equivalently, Pareto Type II with zero location) is \
defined by its survival function and density, with shape kappa and scale \
lambda:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acfa9215-a297-4819-a4d4-c136053ea82a"],

Cell["\<\
lomaxSurvival[x_, kappa_, lambda_] := (1 + x/lambda)^(-kappa)\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[67]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3b963ed8-6db3-4b70-8b84-24064452d510"],

Cell["\<\
lomaxPDF[x_, kappa_, lambda_] := (kappa/lambda) * (1 + x/lambda)^(-(kappa+1))\
\>", "Input",
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2],
 CellLabel->"In[68]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2f4117c9-4e34-4714-ba26-f531e721297f"],

Cell["\<\
Ta(s), under the substitution kappa=a, lambda=a/sigma, is this exact function \
-- not approximately, not asymptotically, term for term:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9993457442726593`*^9, 3.9993457448817186`*^9}},
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.6, 0.4, 0.2],ExpressionUUID->"678de339-1d86-43ef-853a-9394597b87fe"],

Cell["ourTransmittance[s_, sigma_, a_] := (1 + sigma*s/a)^(-a)", "Input",
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2],
 CellLabel->"In[69]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d82450ae-cd78-4afe-b5fa-a6982930407e"],

Cell["ourPDF[s_, sigma_, a_] := sigma/(1 + sigma*s/a)^(a+1)", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d06b2591-ab49-4404-ae9c-55123d3da50f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Simplify[ourTransmittance[s, sigma, a] - lomaxSurvival[s, a, a/sigma]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[71]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d00fc7b8-6c0a-4c78-ac53-e475ad376844"],

Cell[BoxData["0"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999345392734245*^9, 3.9993470378284407`*^9, 
  3.9993481254682493`*^9, 3.999350516529619*^9, 3.999350894716154*^9, 
  3.9993512081060157`*^9, 3.9993512485069113`*^9, 3.9993556938263397`*^9, 
  3.999357100140047*^9, 3.999357831029282*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[71]=",ExpressionUUID->"a7d913bb-8784-4445-b762-68445a7a775e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["(* Expect: 0 *)", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:=",ExpressionUUID->"94a86f8e-a695-407a-b58d-6d36b47163c1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simplify[ourPDF[s, sigma, a] - lomaxPDF[s, a, a/sigma]]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5bc0db93-99a5-4016-86e7-38f841e565ca"],

Cell[BoxData["0"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9993453927968407`*^9, 3.9993470378728595`*^9, 
  3.999348125513144*^9, 3.999350516568617*^9, 3.9993508947494454`*^9, 
  3.999351208149674*^9, 3.9993512485421796`*^9, 3.9993556938673587`*^9, 
  3.9993571001742973`*^9, 3.999357831060398*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[73]=",ExpressionUUID->"3bf726f8-584b-4c43-a941-af2013c71507"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["(* Expect: 0 *)", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7a2ff7eb-dd62-4861-953b-a9489e2fa5f9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gamma Fnc (Davis-Xu)", "Subchapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9993456843710585`*^9, {3.9993458252642145`*^9, 3.9993458340013*^9}, {
   3.9993495239268155`*^9, 3.9993495339188805`*^9}, {3.9993570785016747`*^9, 
   3.999357081238376*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9a7526f8-28b4-4cfb-b200-\
d648de7cf483"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["[see \[Rule]BSSRDF \[Rule] TheoreticalFoundation \[Rule] A \
Generalized Linear Transport Model for Spatially-Correlated Stochastic Media]",
  FontSize->12,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.5]],
 "\n\nLet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s quantify the impact of unresolved random spatial \
fluctuations of \[Sigma](x) on macroscopic transport properties.\n\nWe start \
with the statistics of integrals of \[Sigma](x) over the range of distances ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in arbitrary directions \[CapitalOmega], \naka the optical path along a \
straight line between x and x+s\[CapitalOmega] :"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271627934862337`*^9, 3.8271628459358053`*^9}, {
   3.827162909498432*^9, 3.827163002895013*^9}, 3.827163258539373*^9, {
   3.827163298929126*^9, 3.827163338282044*^9}, {3.827163399051441*^9, 
   3.827163534549815*^9}, {3.8271635680952177`*^9, 3.827163584294661*^9}, {
   3.827163626103662*^9, 3.827163632151843*^9}, {3.8271649075678453`*^9, 
   3.8271649111718493`*^9}, 3.99924041471544*^9, {3.999349493459257*^9, 
   3.9993495119094524`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32b2eaf7-94fa-4406-bf48-\
e180e27ad755"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Tau]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", 
      RowBox[{"x", "+", "s\[CapitalOmega]"}]}], ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "s"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x", "+", "s\[CapitalOmega]"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "s"}]}]}]}],
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"618fb2f1-d224-456c-8bb2-\
81ad442c4d85"],

Cell["\<\

Characterize statistically the direct transmission factor assuming \
stationarity and isotropy:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.827163645203442*^9, 3.8271636773788643`*^9}, 
   3.827163763396564*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c70466bb-ff39-456a-b002-\
d4bebfd39a02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalTau]", 
    RowBox[{"(", "s", ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"t", "(", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", 
         RowBox[{"x", "+", "s\[CapitalOmega]"}]}], ")"}]}]],
     TraditionalForm], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "avr"]}], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ";", "s"}]}], ")"}], "s"}]]}]}],
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}, {3.827163688742998*^9, 
   3.827163691821802*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"145d983e-b12e-48c5-b37e-\
c76332df8780"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nwhere ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "avr"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3945e669-7fd5-4ae5-b3d4-bbd153f2c1a1"],
 " is the average extinction for uncollided transmission, \nessentially a \
coarse version of the random field \[Sigma](x) smoothed over s"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.827163699813222*^9, 3.8271638058767757`*^9}, {
  3.827163880192934*^9, 
  3.827163888361924*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d334f3b-353e-47b3-ad67-\
eeccbc7f6755"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "avr"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ";", "s"}]}], ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "s"], 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "s"], 
     RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x", "+", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["s", "\[Prime]"], "\[CapitalOmega]"}]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", 
       SuperscriptBox["s", "\[Prime]"]}]}]}]}]}],
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}, {3.827163688742998*^9, 3.827163691821802*^9}, {
   3.827163922899901*^9, 
   3.8271639265008497`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"556175c2-6b81-446f-842e-\
66df31bf92d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nWe assume that the random number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "avr"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cf5868e5-08d7-4bd9-baab-5464a34612df"],
 " is statistically indipendent of s and that its variability, for fixed s, \n\
can be approximated with an ensemble of Gamma-distributed values : "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.827163934598974*^9, {3.827164029256633*^9, 3.82716410987464*^9}, 
   3.827164452235115*^9},ExpressionUUID->"70ab1084-ac31-426b-90ca-\
8f1a2ce7885f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Pr", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", ",", "d\[Sigma]"}], "}"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"a", "/", 
        OverscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "-"]}], ")"}], "a"], "\[CapitalGamma]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", 
     RowBox[{"a", "-", "1"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "a\[Sigma]"}], "/", 
      OverscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "-"]}]], "d\[Sigma]"}]}],
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}, {3.827163688742998*^9, 3.827163691821802*^9}, {
   3.827163922899901*^9, 3.8271639265008497`*^9}, {3.8271641222269793`*^9, 
   3.8271641250814857`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b2ef0de8-0a80-4b4f-a47f-\
c409c5465f38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nwhere ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "-"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4f2935e3-3fd7-499a-888f-a5fc428ccde8"],
 " is the mean and ",
 StyleBox["a ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "is the variability parameter :"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.827164129086575*^9, 
  3.827164168374482*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f2f8488b-6d3d-42d1-91b5-\
c93cd046447f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{"a", "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "2"], "-"], "/", 
      OverscriptBox[
       SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "2"], "-"]}], "-", "1"}]]}],
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}, {3.827163688742998*^9, 3.827163691821802*^9}, {
   3.827163922899901*^9, 3.8271639265008497`*^9}, {3.8271641222269793`*^9, 
   3.8271641250814857`*^9}, {3.827164220685494*^9, 
   3.827164223220291*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e6dab047-badd-4293-9f63-\
38410aeaa452"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nIf ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "avr"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "71d144cf-c8bd-47cc-963d-4282ebc7f8e1"],
 " is Gamma-distributed for fixed s so is their product \[Tau], \nand so \
direct transmission reads as the Laplace characteristic function of this \
Gamma PDF :"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.827164228224037*^9, 3.8271642712040777`*^9}, {
  3.8271643305546017`*^9, 
  3.827164382934895*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cba6f5ae-29b3-4a38-a3f9-\
330120cfa1f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"Ta", 
     RowBox[{"(", "s", ")"}]}],
    FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]], 
   StyleBox["=",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]"], 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
        RowBox[{"-", "\[Sigma]s"}]], "Pr", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", ",", "d\[Sigma]"}], "}"}]}]}],
     FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]], 
    StyleBox["=",
     FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4, 0.2]], 
    StyleBox[
     FractionBox["1", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "+", 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "-"], 
          RowBox[{"s", "/", "a"}]}]}], ")"}], "a"]],
     FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0.5, 0]]}]}],
  FontSize->18]], "DisplayFormula",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8271619966269693`*^9, 3.8271620621242943`*^9}, {
   3.827162099788562*^9, 3.827162321324388*^9}, {3.827162391951661*^9, 
   3.827162413842947*^9}, {3.8271625156348667`*^9, 3.827162555726293*^9}, {
   3.8271626818654823`*^9, 3.8271627487812557`*^9}, {3.827163092986535*^9, 
   3.827163263475648*^9}, 3.827163373561021*^9, {3.827163604253469*^9, 
   3.827163609955379*^9}, {3.827163688742998*^9, 3.827163691821802*^9}, {
   3.827163922899901*^9, 3.8271639265008497`*^9}, {3.8271641222269793`*^9, 
